1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,110
Bored with your life?
对自己的生活感到厌倦了吗？

2
00:00:02,110 --> 00:00:04,730
Dreaming of something different?
梦想着一些不一样的事情？

3
00:00:04,730 --> 00:00:12,380
When I feel like that I look up and wonder what life would be like 400km above my head.
当我有那种感觉时，我会抬头仰望，想象在我头顶上方400公里处的生活会是什么样子。

4
00:00:12,380 --> 00:00:23,590
That's where the International Space Station orbits the Earth, with six astronauts living and working on board, for months at a time.
那就是国际空间站环绕地球运行的地方，有六名宇航员在空间站上面生活和工作，每次一待就是好几个月。

5
00:00:23,590 --> 00:00:25,740
How do they sleep?
他们怎么睡觉呢？

6
00:00:25,740 --> 00:00:32,550
They spend the night floating in a sleeping bag inside a small cubicle on the ceiling.
他们晚上在天花板上的一个小隔间里，躺在睡袋中飘浮着睡觉。

7
00:00:32,550 --> 00:00:44,950
American astronaut Sunita Williams explains: "It's like a little phone booth but it's pretty comfy and it doesn't matter if I turn over and sleep upside down.
美国宇航员苏妮塔・威廉姆斯解释说：“它就像一个小小的电话亭，但相当舒适，而且我翻个身倒立着睡觉也没关系。

8
00:00:44,950 --> 00:00:50,460
I don't have any sensation in my head that tells me I'm upside down."
我的脑袋里没有任何感觉会告诉我自己是倒立着的。”

9
00:00:50,460 --> 00:00:56,830
Brushing your teeth in a place where you can't have a tap or a sink can be a challenge.
在一个没有水龙头和水槽的地方刷牙可能是一项挑战。

10
00:00:56,830 --> 00:01:02,460
Can you imagine the mess that running water would make in zero gravity?
你能想象在零重力环境下流动的水会造成怎样的混乱吗？

11
00:01:02,460 --> 00:01:17,160
Canadian astronaut Chris Hadfield uses a straw to put a big blob of water from a sealed bag onto an ordinary toothbrush and adds a little toothpaste - which he has to swallow when he's done.
加拿大宇航员克里斯・哈德菲尔德用一根吸管从一个密封袋中吸一大滴水，滴在一把普通牙刷上，然后挤上一点牙膏——刷完牙后他还得把牙膏吞咽下去。

12
00:01:17,160 --> 00:01:20,690
Daily exercise is essential.
日常锻炼是必不可少的。

13
00:01:20,690 --> 00:01:31,280
The lack of gravity makes bones more brittle and muscles lose strength – so astronauts are encouraged to work out for at least two hours a day.
缺乏重力会使骨骼变得更加脆弱，肌肉也会失去力量——所以宇航员们被鼓励每天至少锻炼两个小时。

14
00:01:31,280 --> 00:01:40,020
The role of astronauts in the International Space Station is to act as lab technicians for scientists back on Earth.
国际空间站中宇航员的角色是充当地球上科学家们的实验室技术员。

15
00:01:40,020 --> 00:01:51,070
So they spend their time maintaining their environment and performing and monitoring experiments in a confined space about the size of a Boeing 747.
所以他们把时间花在维护他们的生活环境，以及在一个大约波音747飞机大小的密闭空间里进行和监测实验上。

16
00:01:51,070 --> 00:02:08,170
Almost every task is carefully planned by mission control - although most astronauts spend their first days losing stuff until they get used to sticking everything they use to the walls with Velcro, duct tape or clips.
几乎每一项任务都由指挥中心精心规划——不过大多数宇航员在最初的几天里总是丢东西，直到他们习惯了用魔术贴、胶带或夹子把他们使用的所有东西都固定在墙上。

17
00:02:08,170 --> 00:02:20,140
One of their most valued perks is the view from "the office", dominated by that gigantic blue ball down there, sitting in the darkness of space.
他们最珍视的福利之一是从“办公室”看到的景色，在黑暗的太空中，映入眼帘的主要是下方那个巨大的蓝色星球。

18
00:02:20,140 --> 00:02:21,780
Wow!
哇！

19
00:02:21,780 --> 00:02:24,140
Absolutely breathtaking!
真是令人叹为观止！
